  "title": "CoRE-UIR and DAR-Net: Unified Framework for All-in-One Image Restoration",
  "summary": "CoRE-UIR and DAR-Net are proposed to address challenges in all-in-one image restoration by combining prior-guided global-local decomposition with dual-ambiguity rectification. CoRE-UIR improves PSNR by 1.05 dB and reduces memory by 85.3%, while DAR-Net achieves the best performance on benchmarks with 0.14 dB and 0.34 dB improvements, respectively.",
